			"Message": "perf(Element): Coalesce high-frequency IPC emits and restore webview rendering\n\nSynchronize 11 Element submodules to address IPC saturation during extension boot and fix webview initialization failures.\n\nMountain introduces batched emits for Decoration, Progress, and TreeView handlers, grouping high-frequency notifications (e.g., 6000+ git progress updates) into 16ms frames to prevent WKWebView channel starvation. Implement deduplication for filesystem watchers and single-flight directory walks to reduce kernel resource exhaustion. Standardize IPC variable names to PascalCase and fix URI normalization for workspace paths.\n\nSky adds a placeholder registry for webview creation to prevent silent drops of `set-html` calls before the workbench accessor is ready, and optimizes bridge logging to emit only on first resolution. Wind normalizes trailing slashes in workspace folder URIs to ensure correct relative path resolution for breadcrumbs. Output restores eager paint overrides and re-enables `isolation: isolate` CSS to fix layout issues, while injecting the missing `IWebviewWorkbenchService` to render extension panels like Roo and Claude.\n\nOther submodules (Cocoon, Common, Echo, etc.) sync to include dependency updates (pnpm, wrangler) and maintain consistency. These changes restore input responsiveness during heavy extension activation and ensure reliable rendering of complex extension features.",
			"SHA": "2c22f8655bd12a6dab8acd8eeeb5dceeef95c84f"
		},
